{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/pulls/2002","id":4461002941,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJvfjJM8AAAABCeWAvQ","html_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/pull/2002","diff_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/pull/2002.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/pull/2002.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/issues/2002","number":2002,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add ERC: Preregistered Acceptance Criteria","user":{"login":"richard7463","id":13402558,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNDAyNTU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13402558?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463","html_url":"https://github.com/richard7463","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richard7463/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nThis PR adds a draft ERC for Preregistered Acceptance Criteria.\n\nExisting agent verification standards reach a verdict by recomputation: derive\nthe artifact again and compare digests. That only works where a verdict is a\nfunction of the artifact. Most of what agents pay for is judged rather than\ncomputed — a generated deliverable, a human review, an on-site inspection.\n\nThis ERC freezes acceptance criteria and typed evidence obligations on-chain\nbefore evidence exists, and requires the final attestation to be itemized\nagainst that frozen list (MET / WAIVED / UNMET / NOT_APPLICABLE). A verdict that\ndeclares an outcome satisfied while a required obligation is recorded UNMET is\nrejected at the contract level rather than merely flagged; so is a verdict that\nrecords failure while no obligation is unmet.\n\nScope is deliberately narrow: registry interface, three off-chain document\nschemas (criteria, evidence bundle, attestation), a packed itemized-verdict\nencoding, and contract-enforced consistency. Evidence formats, payment, and\nidentity are out of scope, so it composes with existing standards (ERC-8126\nverdicts, ERC-8183 settlement, ERC-8004\nidentity) instead of competing with them.\n\n## Discussion\n\nEthereum Magicians: https://ethereum-magicians.org/t/erc-8412-preregistered-acceptance-criteria/29609\n\n## Validation\n\n- Preamble follows EIP-1 (title/description length, discussions-to, type,\n  category, created, requires).\n- Draft content reviewed against the recomputation boundary and the\n  outcome-switching literature (ICMJE registration, COMPare) cited in the\n  motivation.\n- Reference implementation and conformance vectors in `assets/erc-8412/`:\n  registry contract, executable model, reference off-chain verifier, 43 on-chain\n  cases (E1–E14) with a generated Foundry suite, 23 off-chain document packages\n  (O1–O5), and a mutation test confirming every invariant is exercised.\n  `python assets/erc-8412/tools/run_all.py` runs all checks without dependencies.\n","created_at":"2026-09-07T06:41:26Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T15:13:10Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"213a7e002edab8c529962bb46fed4df4276e55e4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"eip-review-bot","id":128646734,"node_id":"U_kgDOB6r-Tg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128646734?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eip-review-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/eip-review-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eip-review-bot/